# Module 14 — Molecular Dynamics

A short MD simulation that produces dynamic descriptors for every site
predicted by Modules 03–05.

---

## What it adds to the pipeline

| Static (Modules 01–13) | Dynamic (Module 14) |
|------------------------|---------------------|
| Active site residues   | RMSF, stability score per site |
| Binding pocket lining  | Pocket volume drift (cryptic-pocket signal) |
| Allosteric site geom.  | Allosteric site flexibility |
| Chemical environment   | H-bond persistence over time |
| Single conformer       | Ensemble (Rg trace, RMSD vs frame 0) |

---

## Install (one extra dep)

Add to `requirements.txt`:

```
openmm>=8.1
```

Then re-run `setup.bat` (or just `pip install openmm` inside the activated
`.venv`). OpenMM ships pre-built CUDA binaries — your RTX 5060 will be
auto-detected.

Verify:
```bat
python -c "import openmm; print(openmm.Platform.getPlatformByName('CUDA').getName())"
```

---

## Run it

Standalone, uses `data/structures/<UID>.pdb` from Module 01 and any site
JSONs already present in `data/intermediate/`:

```bat
:: Quick test — implicit solvent, 1 ns, ~30 s on CPU
python pipeline\14_molecular_dynamics.py --uniprot P04637 --implicit

:: Production — explicit solvent + ions, 5 ns on GPU, ~5 min on RTX 5060
python pipeline\14_molecular_dynamics.py --uniprot P04637 --ns 5
```

Output:
```
data/intermediate/P04637_md.json          ← descriptors (consumed by Module 13)
data/intermediate/md/P04637_traj.dcd      ← trajectory
data/intermediate/md/P04637_top.pdb       ← reference topology
```

